51 miles.\nNow, we need to calculate the total time it takes to cover the entire city. The total distance of the city is 56 miles, and we already know that it takes 234 minutes to cover every 14 miles. Therefore, we can set up another proportion:\n234 minutes / 14 miles = y minutes / 56 miles\nTo solve for y, we can cross-multiply and divide:\ny = (234 minutes * 56 miles) / 14 miles\ny = 924 minutes\nSo, it will take 924 minutes for the fog bank to cover the entire city.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 924.0, "ground_truth": 936.0, "is_correct": false}
{"dataset": "GSM_Distracted", "item_id": 17, "question": "A fog bank rolls in from the ocean to cover a city. It takes 30 minutes to cover every 21 miles of the city, even though 5 miles of the city are parks with no buildings. If the city is 63 miles across from the oceanfront to the opposite inland edge, how many minutes will it take for the fog bank to cover the whole city?", "prompt": "As an expert problem solver, solve step by step the following mathematical questions. A fog bank rolls in from the ocean to cover a city. It takes 30 minutes to cover every 21 miles of the city, even though 5 miles of the city are parks with no buildings. If the city is 63 miles across from the oceanfront to the opposite inland edge, how many minutes will it take for the fog bank to cover the whole city?", "model_response": "<think>\nTo solve this problem, we need to determine the effective distance the fog bank covers and then calculate the time it takes to cover that distance. The city is 63 miles across, but 5 miles of it are parks. Therefore, the fog bank only needs to cover 63 - 5 = 58 miles of the city. The fog bank covers 21 miles in 30 minutes. We need to find out how long it will take to cover 58 miles at the same rate.\n</think>\n<answer>\nTo find out how long it will take to cover 58 miles, we can set up a proportion based on the given information. If 21 miles take 30 minutes, then 58 miles will take \\( x \\) minutes. We can write this as:\n\\[ \\frac{21 \\text{ miles}}{30 \\text{ minutes}} = \\frac{58 \\text{ miles}}{x \\text{ minutes}} \\]\n\nCross-multiplying to solve for \\( x \\):\n\\[ 21x = 58 \\times 30 \\]\n\\[ 21x = 1740 \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{1740}{21} \\]\n\\[ x = 82.8571 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\nTherefore, it will take approximately 82.86 minutes for the fog bank to cover the whole city.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 82.86, "ground_truth": 90.0, "is_correct": false}
{"dataset": "GSM_Distracted", "item_id": 18, "question": "A fog bank rolls in from the ocean to cover a city. It takes 323 minutes to cover every 10 miles of the city. The city has 5 main districts, but 2 of them are smaller in area. If the city is 70 miles across from the oceanfront to the opposite inland edge, how many minutes will it take for the fog bank to cover the whole city?", "prompt": "As an expert problem solver, solve step by step the following mathematical questions. A fog bank rolls in from the ocean to cover a city. It takes 323 minutes to cover every 10 miles of the city. The city has 5 main districts, but 2 of them are smaller in area. If the city is 70 miles across from the oceanfront to the opposite inland edge, how many minutes will it take for the fog bank to cover the whole city?", "model_response": "<think>\nTo solve this problem, we need to break it down into several steps. First, we need to determine the total length of the city that the fog bank needs to cover. The city is 70 miles across from the oceanfront to the inland edge, and it has 5 main districts. However, 2 of these districts are smaller in area, so we need to account for the total length of the city.\n\nSince the city is 70 miles across, the fog bank needs to cover the entire length of the city. The fog bank covers 10 miles in 323 minutes. We need to find out how long it will take to cover 70 miles.\n\nWe can set up a proportion to find the time it takes to cover 70 miles:\n\\[\n\\frac{323 \\text{ minutes}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{x \\text{ minutes}}{70 \\text{ miles}}\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\\[\nx = \\frac{323 \\times 70}{10}\n\\]\n\nLet's calculate this step by step:\n\\[\n323 \\times 70 = 22610\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{22610}{10} = 2261\n\\]\n\nSo, it will take 2261 minutes for the fog bank to cover the entire city.\n</think>\n<answer>\nIt will take 2261 minutes for the fog bank to cover the entire city.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 2261.0, "ground_truth": 2261.0, "is_correct": true}
