g after birds ate some:\n   \\[\n   1925 \\text{ watermelons} - 8 \\text{ watermelons} = 1917 \\text{ watermelons}\n   \\]\n\n3. Number of harvests in a year:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{12 \\text{ months}}{2 \\text{ months per harvest}} = 6 \\text{ harvests}\n   \\]\n\n4. Total watermelons harvested in a year:\n   \\[\n   6 \\text{ harvests} \\times 1925 \\text{ watermelons/harvest} = 11550 \\text{ watermelons}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, Ali can harvest a total of 11,550 watermelons within a year.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 11550.0, "ground_truth": 11550.0, "is_correct": true}
