al weight of corns:**\n   - The farmer buys 31 packs of corns, each weighing 41 kg.\n   - Total weight of corns = 31 packs * 41 kg/pack = 1271 kg\n\n4. **Calculate the total weight of wheats:**\n   - The farmer buys 15 sacks of wheats, each weighing 19 kg.\n   - Total weight of wheats = 15 sacks * 19 kg/sack = 285 kg\n\n5. **Calculate the total weight of all feed items:**\n   - Total weight = Weight of oats + Weight of cucumbers + Weight of corns + Weight of wheats\n   - Total weight = 35 kg + 99 kg + 1271 kg + 285 kg = 1690 kg\n\n6. **Determine the number of trips needed:**\n   - The truck can carry 130 kg at a time.\n   - Number of trips = Total weight / Weight per trip\n   - Number of trips = 1690 kg / 130 kg/trip = 13.00 trips\n\nSince the number of trips must be a whole number, we need to round up to the nearest whole number because even a fraction of a trip would require an additional trip to transport the remaining feed.\n\nTherefore, the farmer needs 14 trips to transport all the feed.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe farmer needs 14 trips to transport all the feed.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 14.0, "ground_truth": 13.0, "is_correct": false}
