e total weight of all the feed:**\n   - Total weight = 20 pounds (wheats) + 105 pounds (beets) + 1,235 pounds (hay) + 240 pounds (corns)\n   - Total weight = 1,590 pounds\n\n3. **Determine the number of trips needed:**\n   - The truck can carry 200 pounds at a time.\n   - Number of trips = Total weight / Capacity of the truck\n   - Number of trips = 1,590 pounds / 200 pounds/trip\n\n4. **Calculate the number of trips:**\n   - Number of trips = 1,590 / 200 = 7.95 trips\n   - Since the number of trips must be a whole number, we need to round up to the next whole number because even a fraction of a trip means an additional trip is needed.\n\n5. **Finalize the number of trips:**\n   - Number of trips = 8 trips\n\nTherefore, the farmer needs to make 8 trips to transport all the feed.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe farmer needs to make 8 trips to transport all the feed.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 8.0, "ground_truth": 9.0, "is_correct": false}
{"dataset": "GSM_Distracted", "item_id": 73, "question": "A farmer is buying feed for his alpacas. He buys a variety of apples, wheats, cucumbers, and corns. Since corns are a rare treat, he only buys six 3-pound boxes of them for the whole stable. He only wants enough cucumbers to feed the alpacas while the vegetables are fresh, so he buys thirteen 9-pound bags. Apples are the main diet of his alpacas, so he buys thirty-five 39-pound packs. Wheats are a staple to supplement the apples, so he buys twenty 15-pound sacks. Although he set aside four 5-pound bags of hay for the horses, those are not part of this trip. If his farm truck can carry 100 pounds at a time, how many trips does the farmer need to transport all the feed?", "prompt": "As an expert problem solver, solve step by step the following mathematical questions. A farmer is buying feed for his alpacas. He buys a variety of apples, wheats, cucumbers, and corns. Since corns are a rare treat, he only buys six 3-pound boxes of them for the whole stable. He only wants enough cucumbers to feed the alpacas while the vegetables are fresh, so he buys thirteen 9-pound bags. Apples are the main diet of his alpacas, so he buys thirty-five 39-pound packs. Wheats are a staple to supplement the apples, so he buys twenty 15-pound sacks. Although he set aside four 5-pound bags of hay for the horses, those are not part of this trip. If his farm truck can carry 100 pounds at a time, how many trips does the farmer need to transport all the feed?", "model_response": "<think>\nTo solve this problem, we need to calculate the total weight of all the feed items the farmer is buying and then determine how many trips the truck needs to make to transport all the feed. Let's break it down step by step:\n\n1. **Corn**: The farmer buys six 3-pound boxes of corn.\n   - Total weight of corn = 6 boxes * 3 pounds/box = 18 pounds\n\n2. **Cucumbers**: The farmer buys thirteen 9-pound bags of cucumbers.\n   - Total weight of cucumbers = 13 bags * 9 pounds/bag = 117 pounds\n\n3. **Apples**: The farmer buys thirty-five 39-pound packs of apples.\n   - Total weight of apples = 35 packs * 39 pounds/pack = 1365 pounds\n\n4. **Wheats**: The farmer buys twenty 15-pound sacks of wheats.\n   - Total weight of wheats = 20 sacks * 15 pounds/sack = 300 pounds\n\n5. **Hay**: The farmer sets aside four 5-pound bags of hay for the horses, but these are not part of the feed for the alpacas.\n   - Total weight of hay = 4 bags * 5 pounds/bag = 20 pounds\n\nNow, let's sum up the total weight of all the feed items:\n- Total weight of feed = Weight of corn + Weight of cucumbers + Weight of apples + Weight of wheats\n- Total weight of feed = 18 pounds + 117 pounds + 1365 pounds + 300 pounds = 1790 pounds\n\nThe truck can carry 100 pounds at a time. To find out how many trips are needed, we divide the total weight by the truck's capacity and round up to the nearest whole number (since partial trips are not possible):\n- Number of trips = Total weight of feed / Truck capacity\n- Number of trips = 1790 pounds / 100 pounds/trip = 17.9 trips\n\nSince the number of trips must be a whole number, we round up to the next whole number:\n- Number of trips = 18 trips\n\nTherefore, the farmer needs to make 18 trips to transport all the feed.\n</think>\n<answer>18 trips</answer>", "model_answer": 18.0, "ground_truth": 18.0, "is_correct": true}
