0 kg (beets) + 1155 kg (wheats) + 255 kg (apples) = 1490 kg\nSince the truck can carry 100 kg at a time, we need to divide the total weight by the truck's capacity to find out how many trips are needed:\nNumber of trips = Total weight / Truck capacity = 1490 kg / 100 kg/trip = 14.9 trips\nSince the number of trips must be a whole number, we need to round up to the nearest whole number, as the truck cannot make a fraction of a trip. Therefore, the farmer needs to make 15 trips to transport all the feed.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe farmer needs to make 15 trips to transport all the feed.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 15.0, "ground_truth": 15.0, "is_correct": true}
