 35 kg\n     \\[\n     35 \\times 35 = 1225 \\text{ kg}\n     \\]\n   - **Corns:** 16 sacks, each 16 kg\n     \\[\n     16 \\times 16 = 256 \\text{ kg}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Sum the total weight of all the feed items:**\n   \\[\n   21 + 98 + 1225 + 256 = 1600 \\text{ kg}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine the number of trips needed:**\n   The truck can carry 200 kg at a time. To find the number of trips required, we divide the total weight by the truck's capacity and round up to the nearest whole number (since partial trips are not possible):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1600}{200} = 8\n   \\]\n\nSince 1600 kg divided by 200 kg per trip results in exactly 8 trips, the farmer needs to make 8 trips to transport all the feed.\n\n4. **Final Answer:**\n   The farmer needs to make \\boxed{8} trips to transport all the feed.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe farmer needs to make 8 trips to transport all the feed.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 8.0, "ground_truth": 8.0, "is_correct": true}
