f carrots = 13 bags * 9 pounds/bag = 117 pounds.\n\n3. **Calculate the total weight of the corns:**\n   - The farmer buys 32 packs of corn, each weighing 43 pounds.\n   - Total weight of corns = 32 packs * 43 pounds/pack = 1376 pounds.\n\n4. **Calculate the total weight of the wheats:**\n   - The farmer buys 15 sacks of wheat, each weighing 15 pounds.\n   - Total weight of wheats = 15 sacks * 15 pounds/sack = 225 pounds.\n\n5. **Calculate the total weight of all the feed items:**\n   - Total weight = Weight of apples + Weight of carrots + Weight of corns + Weight of wheats\n   - Total weight = 42 pounds + 117 pounds + 1376 pounds + 225 pounds = 1750 pounds.\n\n6. **Determine the number of trips needed:**\n   - The truck can carry 110 pounds at a time.\n   - Number of trips = Total weight / Weight per trip\n   - Number of trips = 1750 pounds / 110 pounds/trip\n\n   Since the number of trips must be a whole number, we need to round up to the nearest whole number if there's any remainder.\n\n   Let's perform the division:\n   - 1750 / 110 = 15.909090909090908\n\n   Since 15.909090909090908 is not a whole number, we round up to 16.\n\nTherefore, the farmer needs 16 trips to transport all the feed.\n</think>\n<answer>16 trips</answer>", "model_answer": 16.0, "ground_truth": 16.0, "is_correct": true}
