*\n   - Subtract the total water used from the initial 330 ounces of water.\n\nLet's perform these calculations:\n</think>\n<answer>\n1. **Giant cubes:**\n   - 11 * 12 = 132 ounces\n\n2. **Small cubes:**\n   - 24 * (1/4) = 6 ounces\n   - 5 * (1/4) = 1.25 ounces\n   - 6 - 1.25 = 4.75 ounces\n\n3. **Medium cubes:**\n   - 12 * 11 = 132 ounces\n\n4. **Total water used:**\n   - 132 (giant) + 4.75 (small) + 132 (medium) = 268.75 ounces\n\n5. **Water left:**\n   - 330 - 268.75 = 61.25 ounces\n\nTherefore, Mateo has 61.25 ounces of water left.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 61.25, "ground_truth": 60.0, "is_correct": false}
