{"dataset": "GSM_Distracted", "item_id": 130, "question": "Elena is an avid gardener. Last night, she received 33 new potted plants from her favorite plant nursery. She already has 12 potted plants on each of the 66 window ledges of her large country home, though 5 of those ledges have slightly smaller pots that can only hold 10 plants each. Feeling generous, she has decided that she will give 7 potted plants from each ledge to friends and family tomorrow. How many potted plants will Elena remain with?", "prompt": "As an expert problem solver, solve step by step the following mathematical questions. Elena is an avid gardener. Last night, she received 33 new potted plants from her favorite plant nursery. She already has 12 potted plants on each of the 66 window ledges of her large country home, though 5 of those ledges have slightly smaller pots that can only hold 10 plants each. Feeling generous, she has decided that she will give 7 potted plants from each ledge to friends and family tomorrow. How many potted plants will Elena remain with?", "model_response": "<think>\nTo solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of potted plants Elena currently has.\n2. Determine the number of potted plants that can be placed on the smaller pots.\n3. Calculate the number of potted plants that can be placed on the larger pots.\n4. Subtract the number of potted plants she plans to give away from the total number she currently has.\n\nLet's break it down:\n\n1. **Total number of potted plants currently:**\n   - 12 potted plants on each of the 61 larger pots (66 total ledges - 5 smaller pots).\n   - 10 potted plants on each of the 5 smaller pots.\n   \n   Total = (12 * 61) + (10 * 5)\n\n2. **Number of potted plants that can be placed on the smaller pots:**\n   - 10 potted plants per smaller pot.\n   - 5 smaller pots.\n\n3. **Number of potted plants that can be placed on the larger pots:**\n   - 12 potted plants per larger pot.\n   - 61 larger pots.\n\n4. **Total number of potted plants Elena will give away:**\n   - 7 potted plants per ledge.\n   - 66 ledges.\n\nLet's calculate these step by step.\n</think>\n<answer>\nNow, let's perform the calculations:\n\n1. **Total number of potted plants currently:**\n   \\[\n   12 \\times 61 + 10 \\times 5 = 732 + 50 = 782\n   \\]\n\n2. **Number of potted plants that can be placed on the smaller pots:**\n   \\[\n   10 \\times 5 = 50\n   \\]\n\n3. **Number of potted plants that can be placed on the larger pots:**\n   \\[\n   12 \\times 61 = 732\n   \\]\n\n4. **Total number of potted plants Elena will give away:**\n   \\[\n   7 \\times 66 = 462\n   \\]\n\nNow, let's find out how many potted plants Elena will remain with:\n\\[\n782 - 462 = 320\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Elena will remain with 320 potted plants.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 320.0, "ground_truth": 363.0, "is_correct": false}
