= 3 questions\n2. Algebra questions: Kimia answered 12 questions in the first 20 minutes, and she is sure to get 1/9 of the algebra questions correct.\n   - Correct algebra questions: 1/9 * 23 ≈ 2.55 ≈ 2 questions (since we can't have a fraction of a question, we'll assume 2 questions)\n3. Chemistry questions: Kimia answered 12 questions in the first 20 minutes, and she is sure to get 1/9 of the chemistry questions correct.\n   - Correct chemistry questions: 1/9 * 23 ≈ 2.55 ≈ 2 questions (since we can't have a fraction of a question, we'll assume 2 questions)\n\nFinally, we sum the correct answers to find out how many points she is sure to get:\nTotal correct answers = Correct geography questions + Correct algebra questions + Correct chemistry questions\nTotal correct answers = 3 + 2 + 2 = 7 questions\n\nTherefore, Kimia is sure to get 7 points.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 7.0, "ground_truth": 8.0, "is_correct": false}
