ir members or part of the debate team = 31% of 108 = \\( 0.31 \\times 108 = 33.48 \\).\n   - Since the number of students must be a whole number, we round 33.48 to 33 (assuming rounding to the nearest whole number).\n\n5. **Calculate the total number of students leaving early:**\n   - Students who are only basketball players = 17.\n   - Students who are choir members or part of the debate team = 33.\n   - Total students leaving early = 17 + 33 = 50.\n\nTherefore, the total number of students leaving early is 50.\n</think>\n<answer>50 students are leaving early.</answer>", "model_answer": 50.0, "ground_truth": 56.0, "is_correct": false}
