The students leaving early are those who are swimmers and those who are dancers or part of the robotics club. We add these two groups together:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Total students leaving early} = \\text{Number of swimmers} + \\text{Number of dancers or robotics club members}\n     \\]\n\nNow, let's perform the calculations step by step:\n\n1. **Calculate the number of swimmers:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of swimmers} = 0.40 \\times 125 = 50\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the number of non-swimmers:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of non-swimmers} = 125 - 50 = 75\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the number of dancers or robotics club members:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of dancers or robotics club members} = 0.16 \\times 75 = 12\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum the number of students leaving early:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total students leaving early} = 50 + 12 = 62\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of students leaving early is 62.\n</think>\n<answer>\n62 students are leaving early.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 62.0, "ground_truth": 62.0, "is_correct": true}
