0\n   Agent fee = $23,200\n\n3. Sum the registration fees and the agent fee to get the total expenses:\n   Total expenses = Registration fees + Agent fee\n   Total expenses = $11,600 + $23,200\n   Total expenses = $34,800\n\n4. Subtract the total expenses from the selling price to find the net proceeds:\n   Net proceeds = Selling price - Total expenses\n   Net proceeds = $580,000 - $34,800\n   Net proceeds = $545,200\n\n5. Subtract the remaining loan amount from the net proceeds to get the final net proceeds:\n   Final net proceeds = Net proceeds - Remaining loan amount\n   Final net proceeds = $545,200 - $170,000\n   Final net proceeds = $375,200\n\nTherefore, Prof. Brown's net proceeds from selling the villa is $375,200.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 375200.0, "ground_truth": 375200.0, "is_correct": true}
