nds = 15 * 21 = ₺315\n   - Cost for 9 pounds = 9 * 21 = ₺189\n   - Cost for 1 set of 15 pounds = ₺315 - ₺189 = ₺126\n\n2. Calculate the cost for the remaining 4 pounds:\n   - Since the fudge is on sale, she gets 6 pounds 1/2 off for every 15 pounds.\n   - For 4 pounds, she gets 2 pounds 1/2 off.\n   - Cost for 4 pounds = 4 * 21 = ₺84\n   - Discount for 2 pounds 1/2 = 2.5 * 21 = ₺52.5\n   - Net cost for 4 pounds = ₺84 - ₺52.5 = ₺31.5\n\n3. Calculate the total cost of the fudge:\n   - Total cost = Cost for 1 set of 15 pounds + Net cost for 4 pounds\n   - Total cost = ₺126 + ₺31.5 = ₺157.5\n\nNext, let's calculate the cost of the sand dollars and postcards:\n4. Cost of sand dollars = ₺11.5\n5. Cost of postcards = 15 * ₺20.5 = ₺307.5\n\nNow, let's calculate the total cost of all items:\n6. Total cost = Cost of fudge + Cost of sand dollars + Cost of postcards\n7. Total cost = ₺157.5 + ₺11.5 + ₺307.5 = ₺476.5\n\nFinally, let's calculate how much money Keisha has left:\n8. Money left = Initial amount - Total cost\n9. Money left = ₺1400 - ₺476.5 = ₺923.5\n\nTherefore, Keisha has ₺923.5 left.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 923.5, "ground_truth": 661.0, "is_correct": false}
