s, we need to calculate the cost for 18 pounds:\n\\[ 18 \\text{ pounds} \\times \\$22/\\text{pound} = \\$396 \\]\n\nNext, we need to account for the discount. The discount is for 6 pounds and 2/3 off. The cost for 6 pounds is:\n\\[ 6 \\text{ pounds} \\times \\$22/\\text{pound} = \\$132 \\]\n\nThe discount is 2/3 off, so the discount amount is:\n\\[ \\frac{2}{3} \\times \\$132 = \\$88 \\]\n\nTherefore, the cost after the discount is:\n\\[ \\$132 - \\$88 = \\$44 \\]\n\nNow, we add the cost of the 12 pounds (18 - 6) that are not discounted:\n\\[ 12 \\text{ pounds} \\times \\$22/\\text{pound} = \\$264 \\]\n\nSo, the total cost for the rock candy is:\n\\[ \\$44 + \\$264 = \\$308 \\]\n\nKimia also bought a mixed bag of sea glass for $11.75 and 17 stickers that were $21.25 each. The cost for the stickers is:\n\\[ 17 \\text{ stickers} \\times \\$21.25/\\text{sticker} = \\$361.25 \\]\n\nNow, we add up all the costs:\n\\[ \\text{Cost of rock candy} + \\text{Cost of sea glass} + \\text{Cost of stickers} = \\$308 + \\$11.75 + \\$361.25 = \\$681 \\]\n\nFinally, we subtract the total cost from the initial $1300 to find out how much money Kimia has left:\n\\[ \\$1300 - \\$681 = \\$619 \\]\n\nTherefore, Kimia has $619 left.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 619.0, "ground_truth": 509.0, "is_correct": false}
