ts = 4\nEffective planting area = 213 - (4 * 17.75) - 7\nLet's calculate this:\n</think>\n<answer>\nEffective planting area = 213 - (4 * 17.75) - 7\nEffective planting area = 213 - 71 - 7\nEffective planting area = 135 meters\nNow, let's move to step 2:\nNumber of plants needed = Effective planting area / Width of each plant\nNumber of plants needed = 135 / 7\nNumber of plants needed = 19.2857\nSince we can't have a fraction of a plant, we'll round up to the nearest whole number:\nNumber of plants needed = 20\nNow, let's move to step 3:\nTotal number of plants = Existing plants + Number of new plants needed\nTotal number of plants = 11 + 20\nTotal number of plants = 31\nFinally, let's move to step 4:\nTotal cost = Total number of plants * Cost per plant\nTotal cost = 31 * 11\nTotal cost = ¥341\nTherefore, Chen will spend ¥341 at the store to fill up her flower bed.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 341.0, "ground_truth": 11.0, "is_correct": false}
