tes - Special honors graduates\n   Total graduates = 1350\n   Special honors graduates = 150\n   Regular graduates = 1350 - 150 = 1200\n\n5. Tickets per regular graduate = Seats available for regular graduates / Number of regular graduates\n   Tickets per regular graduate = 6600 / 1200 = 5.5\n\nSince we can't give half a ticket, we need to round down to the nearest whole number. Therefore, each regular graduate will receive 5 tickets.\n</think>\n<answer>\nEach regular graduate will receive 5 tickets.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 5.0, "ground_truth": 5.0, "is_correct": true}
