uates is not specified, we can't provide a numerical answer. However, if we assume there are 'G' graduates, the formula to find out how many tickets each graduate would receive is:\n\n   Tickets per graduate = 4750 / G\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe number of tickets each graduate would receive, if there are 'G' graduates, is given by the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Tickets per graduate} = \\frac{4750}{G} \\]\n\nWithout knowing the exact number of graduates (G), we cannot provide a specific numerical answer. If you provide the number of graduates, we can calculate the exact number of tickets each graduate would receive.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 4750.0, "ground_truth": 5.0, "is_correct": false}
