{"dataset": "GSM_Distracted", "item_id": 467, "question": "Greenville High School is holding graduation in their Convention Center this year which has space for 7000 people. The event will last for 3 hours, and there will be 750 seats reserved for graduates and 250 seats for faculty attending. How many tickets would each graduate receive to give to their friends and family if the tickets are split equally?", "prompt": "As an expert problem solver, solve step by step the following mathematical questions. Greenville High School is holding graduation in their Convention Center this year which has space for 7000 people. The event will last for 3 hours, and there will be 750 seats reserved for graduates and 250 seats for faculty attending. How many tickets would each graduate receive to give to their friends and family if the tickets are split equally?", "model_response": "<think>\nTo solve this problem, we need to determine the number of tickets each graduate will receive. We start by calculating the total number of seats available for guests, which is the total capacity of the Convention Center minus the reserved seats for graduates and faculty. Then, we divide the remaining seats by the number of graduates to find out how many tickets each graduate will get.\n</think>\n<answer>\nFirst, let's calculate the total number of seats available for guests:\nTotal seats = Total capacity - Reserved seats for graduates - Reserved seats for faculty\nTotal seats = 7000 - 750 - 250 = 6000\n\nNow, we need to find out how many tickets each graduate will receive. We do this by dividing the total number of guest seats by the number of graduates:\nTickets per graduate = Total guest seats / Number of graduates\nTickets per graduate = 6000 / Number of graduates\n\nSince we don't know the exact number of graduates, we can't calculate the exact number of tickets per graduate. However, we can express the number of tickets per graduate in terms of the number of graduates.\n</answer>", "model_