{"dataset": "GSM_Distracted", "item_id": 553, "question": "Priya is learning to write and decides to keep re-writing the hiragana (with 48 letters) until she knows it. She writes it in full eight times, writes 1/2 of it once, and although she takes 15 minutes for each full writing, she then re-writes everything she has already written. How many letters has Priya written in total?", "prompt": "As an expert problem solver, solve step by step the following mathematical questions. Priya is learning to write and decides to keep re-writing the hiragana (with 48 letters) until she knows it. She writes it in full eight times, writes 1/2 of it once, and although she takes 15 minutes for each full writing, she then re-writes everything she has already written. How many letters has Priya written in total?", "model_response": "<think>\nTo solve this problem, let's break it down step by step:\n\n1. **Total number of hiragana letters**: There are 48 hiragana letters.\n\n2. **First part of the problem**: Priya writes the hiragana in full eight times.\n   - Each full writing takes 15 minutes.\n   - Total letters written in this part = 48 letters per writing * 8 writings = 384 letters.\n\n3. **Second part of the problem**: Priya writes 1/2 of the hiragana once.\n   - Half of 48 letters = 48 / 2 = 24 letters.\n   - Total letters written in this part = 24 letters.\n\n4. **Third part of the problem**: Priya re-writes everything she has already written.\n   - This includes the 384 letters from the first part and the 24 letters from the second part.\n   - Total letters re-written = 384 + 24 = 408 letters.\n\n5. **Total letters written**: Sum up all the letters written in each part.\n   - Total letters = 384 (first part) + 24 (second part) + 408 (re-written) = 816 letters.\n\nTherefore, the total number of letters Priya has written is 816.\n</think>\n<answer>816</answer>", "model_answer": 816.0, "ground_truth": 816.0, "is_correct": true}
