{"dataset": "GSM_Distracted", "item_id": 658, "question": "Aisha is trying to decide whether to do her business accounting herself or hire one bookkeeper. If she does it herself, she'll be able to do 9 fewer hours of contract work, losing €33/hour in missed income. She usually works 40 hours a week, but last week she took 2 days off. The bookkeeper charges €187. How much more money will she have if she hires the bookkeeper?", "prompt": "As an expert problem solver, solve step by step the following mathematical questions. Aisha is trying to decide whether to do her business accounting herself or hire one bookkeeper. If she does it herself, she'll be able to do 9 fewer hours of contract work, losing €33/hour in missed income. She usually works 40 hours a week, but last week she took 2 days off. The bookkeeper charges €187. How much more money will she have if she hires the bookkeeper?", "model_response": "<think>\nTo solve this problem, we need to break it down into several steps. First, we need to determine how many hours Aisha worked last week. Then, we need to calculate the missed income if she does her own accounting. Finally, we need to compare the missed income to the cost of hiring a bookkeeper to find out how much more money she would have if she hires the bookkeeper.\n</think>\n<answer>\nLet's start by calculating the number of hours Aisha worked last week. She usually works 40 hours a week, but she took 2 days off. Assuming a week has 7 days, she worked 5 days last week. So, the number of hours she worked last week is:\n\\[ \\text{Hours worked last week} = 40 \\text{ hours/week} \\times \\frac{5 \\text{ days}}{7 \\text{ days/week}} = \\frac{200}{7} \\approx 28.57 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nNext, we need to calculate the missed income if Aisha does her own accounting. She would lose €33/hour in missed income for the hours she worked last week. So, the missed income is:\n\\[ \\text{Missed income} = 28.57 \\text{ hours} \\times €33/\\text{hour} \\approx €942.61 \\]\