nterviews**: Calculate 27% of the remaining applicants.\n   \\[\n   0.27 \\times 485 = 131.55 \\approx 132 \\text{ applicants receive interviews}\n   \\]\n5. **Applicants Receiving Job Offers**: Calculate 20% of the applicants receiving interviews.\n   \\[\n   0.20 \\times 132 = 26.4 \\approx 26 \\text{ applicants receive job offers}\n   \\]\n6. **Applicants Accepting Job Offers**: Calculate 4/6 (or 2/3) of the applicants receiving job offers.\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2}{3} \\times 26 = \\frac{52}{3} \\approx 17.33 \\approx 17 \\text{ applicants accept the position}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of people who accept the position is approximately 17.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 17.0, "ground_truth": 18.0, "is_correct": false}
