ck needs to make to transport all the feed. Since the truck can carry 200 pounds at a time, we can divide the total weight by the truck's capacity:\nNumber of trips = Total weight / Truck capacity = 1,790 pounds / 200 pounds/trip = 8.95 trips\nSince the number of trips must be a whole number, we need to round up to the nearest whole number. In this case, we need to round up to 9 trips to ensure all the feed is transported.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe farmer needs to make 9 trips to transport all the feed.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 9.0, "ground_truth": 9.0, "is_correct": true, "original_answer_text": "The farmer is buying 5 * 4 = 20 pounds of wheats.\nHe is buying 15 * 7 = 105 pounds of beets.\nHe is buying 15 * 16 = 240 pounds of corns.\nHe is buying 35 * 41 = 1435 pounds of hay.\nThe weight of all the feed is 20 + 105 + 240 + 1435 = 1800 pounds.\nThus, the farmer needs 1800 / 200 = 9 trips to transport all the feed in his farm truck.\n#### 9"}
