:\nTotal weight = 18 pounds (corns) + 117 pounds (cucumbers) + 1365 pounds (apples) + 300 pounds (wheats)\nTotal weight = 18 + 117 + 1365 + 300 = 1800 pounds\n\nNow, we need to determine how many trips the farmer's truck needs to make to transport all the feed, given that the truck can carry 100 pounds at a time:\nNumber of trips = Total weight / Weight per trip\nNumber of trips = 1800 pounds / 100 pounds/trip\nNumber of trips = 18 trips\n\nTherefore, the farmer needs to make 18 trips to transport all the feed.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 18.0, "ground_truth": 18.0, "is_correct": true, "original_answer_text": "The farmer is buying 6 * 3 = 18 pounds of corns.\nHe is buying 13 * 9 = 117 pounds of cucumbers.\nHe is buying 20 * 15 = 300 pounds of wheats.\nHe is buying 35 * 39 = 1365 pounds of apples.\nThe weight of all the feed is 18 + 117 + 300 + 1365 = 1800 pounds.\nThus, the farmer needs 1800 / 100 = 18 trips to transport all the feed in his farm truck.\n#### 18"}
