{"dataset": "GSM_Original", "item_id": 130, "question": "Elena is an avid gardener. Last night, she received 33 new potted plants from her favorite plant nursery. She already has 12 potted plants on each of the 66 window ledges of her large country home. Feeling generous, she has decided that she will give 7 potted plants from each ledge to friends and family tomorrow. How many potted plants will Elena remain with?", "prompt": "As an expert problem solver, solve step by step the following mathematical questions. Elena is an avid gardener. Last night, she received 33 new potted plants from her favorite plant nursery. She already has 12 potted plants on each of the 66 window ledges of her large country home. Feeling generous, she has decided that she will give 7 potted plants from each ledge to friends and family tomorrow. How many potted plants will Elena remain with?", "model_response": "<think>\nTo solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of potted plants Elena currently has.\n2. Determine the total number of potted plants she plans to give away.\n3. Subtract the number of plants given away from the total number of plants she currently has.\n\nLet's break it down:\n\n1. **Total number of potted plants Elena currently has:**\n   - She has 12 potted plants on each of the 66 window ledges.\n   - Total plants = 12 plants/ledge * 66 ledges\n\n2. **Total number of potted plants Elena plans to give away:**\n   - She plans to give 7 potted plants from each of the 66 window ledges.\n   - Total plants to give away = 7 plants/ledge * 66 ledges\n\n3. **Calculate the remaining number of potted plants:**\n   - Remaining plants = Total plants - Total plants to give away\n\nLet's perform the calculations:\n</think>\n<answer>\n1. Total number of potted plants Elena currently has:\n   \\[\n   12 \\text{ plants/ledge} \\times 66 \\text{ ledges} = 792 \\text{ plants}\n   \\]\n\n2. Total number of potted plants Elena plans to give away:\n   \\[\n   7 \\text{ plants/ledge} \\times 66 \\text{ ledges} = 462 \\text{ plants}\n   \\]\n\n3. Remaining number of potted plants:\n   \\[\n   792 \\text{ plants} - 462 \\text{ plants} = 330 \\text{ plants}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, Elena will remain with 330 potted plants.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 330.0, "ground_truth": 363.0, "is_correct": false, "original_answer_text": "Last night, before receiving the plants, Elena had 66*12 = 792 potted plants\nAfter receiving an additional 33 plants, she therefore had a total of 792 + 33 = 825 potted plants\nTomorrow, Elena's plant giveaway will be 66*7 = 462 potted plants.\nShe will therefore remain with 825 - 462 = 363 potted plants.\n#### 363"}
{"dataset": "GSM_Original", "item_id": 131, "question": "Ava is an avid gardener. Two days ago, she received 23 new potted plants from her favorite plant nursery. She already has 8 potted plants on each of the 59 window ledges of her large country home. Feeling generous, she has decided that she will give 7 potted plants from each ledge to friends and family tomorrow. How many potted plants will Ava remain with?", "prompt": "As an expert problem solver, solve step by step the following mathematical questions. Ava is an avid gardener. Two days ago, she received 23 new potted plants from her favorite plant nursery. She already has 8 potted plants on each of the 59 window ledges of her large country home. Feeling generous, she has decided that she will give 7 potted plants from each ledge to friends and family tomorrow. How many potted plants will Ava remain with?", "model_response": "<think>\nTo solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n1. Calculate the total number of potted plants Ava currently has.\n2. Calculate the total number of potted plants Ava will give away.\n3. Subtract the number of plants given away from the total number of plants Ava currently has.\n4. Add the new potted plants she received to the remaining number of plants.\n</think>\n<answer>\nLet's go through these steps one by one:\n\n1. Ava already has 8 potted plants on each of the 59 window ledges. So, the total number of potted plants she currently has is:\n   8 plants/ledge * 59 ledges = 472 plants\n\n2. Ava plans to give 7 potted plants from each of the 59 window ledges to friends and family. So, the total number of potted plants she will give away is:\n   7 plants/ledge * 59 ledges = 413 plants\n\n3. Now, we subtract the number of plants given away from the total number of plants Ava currently has:\n   472 plants - 413 plants = 59 plants\n\n4. Ava received 23 new potted plants from her favorite plant nursery. So, we add these to the remaining number of plants:\n   59 plants + 23 plants = 82 plants\n\nTherefore, Ava will remain with 82 potted plants.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 82.0, "ground_truth": 82.0, "is_correct": true, "original_answer_text": "Two days ago, before receiving the plants, Ava had 59*8 = 472 potted plants\nAfter receiving an additional 23 plants, she therefore had a total of 472 + 23 = 495 potted plants\nTomorrow, Ava's plant giveaway will be 59*7 = 413 potted plants.\nShe will therefore remain with 495 - 413 = 82 potted plants.\n#### 82"}
