ad 69*11 = 759 potted plants\nAfter receiving an additional 38 plants, she therefore had a total of 759 + 38 = 797 potted plants\nTomorrow, Sakura's plant giveaway will be 69*4 = 276 potted plants.\nShe will therefore remain with 797 - 276 = 521 potted plants.\n#### 521"}
{"dataset": "GSM_Original", "item_id": 137, "question": "Fatima is an avid gardener. Last night, she received 21 new potted plants from her favorite plant nursery. She already has 12 potted plants on each of the 63 window ledges of her large country home. Feeling generous, she has decided that she will give 3 potted plants from each ledge to friends and family tomorrow. How many potted plants will Fatima remain with?", "prompt": "As an expert problem solver, solve step by step the following mathematical questions. Fatima is an avid gardener. Last night, she received 21 new potted plants from her favorite plant nursery. She already has 12 potted plants on each of the 63 window ledges of her large country home. Feeling generous, she has decided that she will give 3 potted plants from each ledge to friends and family tomorrow. How many potted plants will Fatima remain with?", "model_response": "<think>\nTo solve this problem, we need to follow a step-by-step approach to determine how many potted plants Fatima will have left after giving some away. Let's break it down:\n\n1. **Initial Count of Plants:**\n   - Fatima already has 12 potted plants on each of the 63 window ledges.\n   - Total initial plants = 12 plants/ledge * 63 ledges\n\n2. **Adding New Plants:**\n   - Fatima received 21 new potted plants last night.\n   - Total plants after receiving new ones = Initial plants + 21\n\n3. **Plants to Give Away:**\n   - Fatima plans to give 3 potted plants from each of the 63 window ledges to friends and family.\n   - Total plants to give away = 3 plants/ledge * 63 ledges\n\n4. **Calculating Remaining Plants:**\n   - Remaining plants = Total plants after receiving new ones - Total plants to give away\n\nLet's perform the calculations:\n\n1. **Initial Count of Plants:**\n   \\[\n   12 \\text{ plants/ledge} \\times 63 \\text{ ledges} = 756 \\text{ plants}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Adding New Plants:**\n   \\[\n   756 \\text{ plants} + 21 \\text{ plants} = 777 \\text{ plants}\n   \\]\n\