{"dataset": "GSM_Original", "item_id": 138, "question": "Aisha is an avid gardener. Last night, she received 36 new potted plants from her favorite plant nursery. She already has 8 potted plants on each of the 54 window ledges of her large country home. Feeling generous, she has decided that she will give 4 potted plants from each ledge to friends and family tomorrow. How many potted plants will Aisha remain with?", "prompt": "As an expert problem solver, solve step by step the following mathematical questions. Aisha is an avid gardener. Last night, she received 36 new potted plants from her favorite plant nursery. She already has 8 potted plants on each of the 54 window ledges of her large country home. Feeling generous, she has decided that she will give 4 potted plants from each ledge to friends and family tomorrow. How many potted plants will Aisha remain with?", "model_response": "<think>\nTo solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n1. Calculate the total number of potted plants Aisha currently has.\n2. Determine the total number of potted plants she will give away.\n3. Subtract the number of potted plants given away from the total number she currently has.\n4. The result will be the number of potted plants Aisha will remain with.\n</think>\n<answer>\nLet's calculate step by step:\n1. Total number of potted plants Aisha currently has:\n   She has 8 potted plants on each of the 54 window ledges.\n   Total = 8 * 54 = 432 potted plants\n\n2. Total number of potted plants she will give away:\n   She plans to give 4 potted plants from each of the 54 window ledges.\n   Total = 4 * 54 = 216 potted plants\n\n3. Number of potted plants Aisha will remain with:\n   Remaining = Total currently - Total given away\n   Remaining = 432 - 216 = 216 potted plants\n</answer>", "model_answer": 216.0, "ground_truth": 252.0, "is_correct": false, "original_answer_text": "Last night, before receiving the plants, Aisha had 54*8 = 432 potted plants\nAfter receiving an additional 36 plants, she therefore had a total of 432 + 36 = 468 potted plants\nTomorrow, Aisha's plant giveaway will be 54*4 = 216 potted plants.\nShe will therefore remain with 468 - 216 = 252 potted plants.\n#### 252"}
{"dataset": "GSM_Original", "item_id": 139, "question": "Sakura is an avid gardener. Last night, she received 29 new potted plants from her favorite plant nursery. She already has 9 potted plants on each of the 56 window ledges of her large country home. Feeling generous, she has decided that she will give 6 potted plants from each ledge to friends and family tomorrow. How many potted plants will Sakura remain with?", "prompt": "As an expert problem solver, solve step by step the following mathematical questions. Sakura is an avid gardener. Last night, she received 29 new potted plants from her favorite plant nursery. She already has 9 potted plants on each of the 56 window ledges of her large country home. Feeling generous, she has decided that she will give 6 potted plants from each ledge to friends and family tomorrow. How many potted plants will Sakura remain with?", "model_response": "<think>\nTo solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n1. Calculate the total number of potted plants Sakura currently has.\n2. Calculate the total number of potted plants she plans to give away.\n3. Subtract the number of plants given away from the total number of plants she currently has.\n4. The result will be the number of potted plants Sakura will remain with.\nLet's start with step 1:\n1. Sakura has 9 potted plants on each of the 56 window ledges. So, the total number of potted plants she currently has is 9 * 56.\n2. For step 2, we need to calculate the total number of potted plants she plans to give away. She plans to give 6 potted plants from each of the 56 window ledges. So, the total number of potted plants she plans to give away is 6 * 56.\n3. For step 3, we subtract the number of plants given away from the total number of plants she currently has.\n4. Finally, we will get the number of potted plants Sakura will remain with.\n</think>\n<answer>\nLet's perform the calculations:\n1. Total current potted plants = 9 * 56 = 504\n2. Total potted plants to give away = 6 * 56 = 336\n3. Remaining potted plants = 504 - 336 = 168\nTherefore, Sakura will remain with 168 potted plants.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 168.0, "ground_truth": 197.0, "is_correct": false, "original_answer_text": "Last night, before receiving the plants, Sakura had 56*9 = 504 potted plants\nAfter receiving an additional 29 plants, she therefore had a total of 504 + 29 = 533 potted plants\nTomorrow, Sakura's plant giveaway will be 56*6 = 336 potted plants.\nShe will therefore remain with 533 - 336 = 197 potted plants.\n#### 197"}
{"dataset": "GSM_Original", "item_id": 140, "question": "Quinn and Sakura have 107 minutes to walk to the library together. It takes them 26 minutes to get to the corner where the mall is. It takes them another 62 minutes to get to the park. How much longer do they have to get to library without being late?", "prompt": "As an expert problem solver, solve step by step the following mathematical questions. Quinn and Sakura have 107 minutes to walk to the library together. It takes them 26 minutes to get to the corner where the mall is. It takes them another 62 minutes to get to the park. How much longer do they have to get to library without being late?", "model_response": "<think>\nTo solve this problem, we need to determine the total time Quinn and Sakura have already spent walking and then subtract that from the total time they have available. We can break this down into a few steps:\n1. Calculate the total time spent walking so far.\n2. Subtract the time spent walking so far from the total time available.\n3. The result will be the remaining time they have to get to the library without being late.\nLet's start with step 1:\nTotal time spent walking so far = Time to the corner + Time to the park\nTotal time spent walking so far = 26 minutes + 62 minutes\nTotal time spent walking so far = 88 minutes\nNow, let's move to step 2:\nRemaining time = Total time available - Total time spent walking so far\nRemaining time = 107 minutes - 88 minutes\nRemaining time = 19 minutes\nTherefore, they have 19 minutes left to get to the library without being late.\n</think>\n<answer>\nQuinn and Sakura have 19 minutes left to get to the library without being late.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 19.0, "ground_truth": 19.0, "is_correct": true, "original_answer_text": "Quinn and Sakura arrive at the mall with 107 - 26 = 81 minutes left to reach the library.\nThey then arrive at the park and have 81 - 62 = 19 minutes left to get to library without being late.\n#### 19"}
