s per minute\nNext, we need to calculate the time it takes her to walk the remaining 13 miles on the sidewalk. We can use the formula:\nTime = Distance / Speed\nTime on the sidewalk = 13 miles / 0.5 miles per minute\nTime on the sidewalk = 26 minutes\nNow, we can calculate the total time it takes her to complete the entire 25-mile walk by summing the time spent on the beach and the time spent on the sidewalk:\nTotal time = Time on the beach + Time on the sidewalk\nTotal time = 48 minutes + 26 minutes\nTotal time = 74 minutes\nTherefore, it takes Fatima 74 minutes to complete the entire 25-mile walk.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 25.0, "ground_truth": 74.0, "is_correct": false, "original_answer_text": "On the beach, Fatima walks at a rate of 12 miles per 48 minutes, or 12/48 = 1/4 miles per minute.\nOn the sidewalk, she walks at 2 times the rate of speed as when she is on the sand, or 2 * 1/4 = 1/2 miles per minute.\nTo walk 13 miles on the sidewalk, it takes her 13÷1/2=26 minutes.\nThus, in total, it takes Fatima 48+26=74 minutes to walk her favorite route.\n#### 74"}
