idewalk is 18 kilometers, so the time spent walking on the sidewalk is:\n\\[ \\text{Time on sidewalk} = \\frac{18}{v_s} = \\frac{18}{\\frac{2}{3}} = 18 \\times \\frac{3}{2} = 27 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\nNow, we can find the total time spent walking by adding the time spent on the beach and the time spent on the sidewalk:\n\\[ \\text{Total time} = 51 + 27 = 78 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\nTherefore, the total time it takes for Uma to complete the entire 35-kilometer walk is:\n\\[ \\boxed{78} \\]\n</think>\n<answer>\n78 minutes\n</answer>", "model_answer": 78.0, "ground_truth": 78.0, "is_correct": true, "original_answer_text": "On the beach, Uma walks at a rate of 17 kilometers per 51 minutes, or 17/51 = 1/3 kilometers per minute.\nOn the sidewalk, she walks at 2 times the rate of speed as when she is on the sand, or 2 * 1/3 = 2/3 kilometers per minute.\nTo walk 18 kilometers on the sidewalk, it takes her 18÷2/3=27 minutes.\nThus, in total, it takes Uma 51+27=78 minutes to walk her favorite route.\n#### 78"}
