 sum the correct answers to find the total number of points she is sure to get:\nTotal points = 3 (algebra) + 15 (physics) + 15 (history) = 33 points\n</answer>", "model_answer": 33.0, "ground_truth": 33.0, "is_correct": true, "original_answer_text": "The physics and history questions comprises 100% - 25% = 75% of the quiz.\nThere are 80 questions x 25/100 = 20 algebra questions.\nThere are a total of 80 questions x 75/100 = 60 physics and history questions.\nIf Daphne is sure to get 15% of the algebra questions, then this means she is sure of her 20 questions x 15/100 = 3 points.\nFrom the physics and history questions, she is sure to get 1/2 of it correctly so that is 60 questions * 1/2 = 30 points.\nThus, she is sure of getting 3 points + 30 points = 33 points in her quiz.\n#### 33"}
