y, we'll sum these correct answers to find the total number of points she is sure to get:\nTotal correct answers = Geography correct + History correct + Chemistry correct\nTotal correct answers = 28 + 15 + 15 = 58 questions\nTherefore, Isabella is sure to get 58 points.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 58.0, "ground_truth": 58.0, "is_correct": true, "original_answer_text": "The history and chemistry questions comprises 100% - 40% = 60% of the quiz.\nThere are 100 questions x 40/100 = 40 geography questions.\nThere are a total of 100 questions x 60/100 = 60 history and chemistry questions.\nIf Isabella is sure to get 70% of the geography questions, then this means she is sure of her 40 questions x 70/100 = 28 points.\nFrom the history and chemistry questions, she is sure to get 1/2 of it correctly so that is 60 questions * 1/2 = 30 points.\nThus, she is sure of getting 28 points + 30 points = 58 points in her quiz.\n#### 58"}
