{10}{100} \\]\n\\[ \\text{Transfer Fee} = 290,000 \\times 0.10 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Transfer Fee} = 29,000 \\]\n\nNow, let's calculate the total price of the house by adding the selling price, the brokerage fee, and the transfer fee:\n\\[ \\text{Total Price} = \\text{Selling Price} + \\text{Brokerage Fee} + \\text{Transfer Fee} \\]\n\\[ \\text{Total Price} = 290,000 + 8,700 + 29,000 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Total Price} = 327,700 \\]\n\nFinally, let's compare the total price to Mrs. Smith's budget of $320,000 to find out how much more the total price exceeds her budget:\n\\[ \\text{Excess Amount} = \\text{Total Price} - \\text{Budget} \\]\n\\[ \\text{Excess Amount} = 327,700 - 320,000 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Excess Amount} = 7,700 \\]\n\nTherefore, the total price of the house exceeds Mrs. Smith's budget by $7,700.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 7700.0, "ground_truth": 7700.0, "is_correct": true, "original_answer_text": "The brokerage fee is $290000 x 3/100 = $8700.\nThe transfer fee is $290000 x 10/100 = $29000.\nThe total price of the house is $290000 + $8700 + $29000 = $327700.\nSo, it is $327700 - $320000 = $7700 more than Mrs. Smith's budget.\n#### 7700"}
