xt{Transfer Fee} = 420,000 \\times 0.11 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Transfer Fee} = 46,200 \\]\n\nNow, let's calculate the total price of the apartment by adding the selling price, the brokerage fee, and the transfer fee:\n\\[ \\text{Total Price} = \\text{Selling Price} + \\text{Brokerage Fee} + \\text{Transfer Fee} \\]\n\\[ \\text{Total Price} = 420,000 + 21,000 + 46,200 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Total Price} = 487,200 \\]\n\nFinally, let's compare the total price to Ms. Johnson's budget of $430,000 to find out how much more it exceeds her budget:\n\\[ \\text{Excess Amount} = \\text{Total Price} - \\text{Budget} \\]\n\\[ \\text{Excess Amount} = 487,200 - 430,000 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Excess Amount} = 57,200 \\]\n\nTherefore, the total price of the apartment exceeds Ms. Johnson's budget by $57,200.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 57200.0, "ground_truth": 57200.0, "is_correct": true, "original_answer_text": "The brokerage fee is $420000 x 5/100 = $21000.\nThe transfer fee is $420000 x 11/100 = $46200.\nThe total price of the apartment is $420000 + $21000 + $46200 = $487200.\nSo, it is $487200 - $430000 = $57200 more than Ms. Johnson's budget.\n#### 57200"}
