 56 minutes because 28 x 2 = 56\n#### 56"}
{"dataset": "GSM_Original", "item_id": 697, "question": "On Saturday, Umar wants to exercise for ten times the amount of time he did on Friday and Thursday combined. On Thursday he exercised for 24 minutes. On Friday he exercised for 16 minutes. How many minutes does he have to exercise on Saturday to reach his goal?", "prompt": "As an expert problem solver, solve step by step the following mathematical questions. On Saturday, Umar wants to exercise for ten times the amount of time he did on Friday and Thursday combined. On Thursday he exercised for 24 minutes. On Friday he exercised for 16 minutes. How many minutes does he have to exercise on Saturday to reach his goal?", "model_response": "<think>\nTo solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total amount of time Umar exercised on Friday and Thursday combined.\n2. Determine the target time Umar wants to exercise on Saturday, which is ten times the combined time from step 1.\n3. Calculate the difference between the target time and the time Umar has already exercised on Friday and Thursday to find out how much more he needs to exercise on Saturday.\n\nLet's break it down:\n\n1. Time exercised on Friday: 16 minutes\n   Time exercised on Thursday: 24 minutes\n   Combined time for Friday and Thursday: 16 + 24 = 40 minutes\n\n2. Target time for Saturday: 10 times the combined time\n   Target time for Saturday = 10 * 40 = 400 minutes\n\n3. Time already exercised on Friday and Thursday: 40 minutes\n   Time needed on Saturday = Target time - Time already exercised\n   Time needed on Saturday = 400 - 40 = 360 minutes\n\nTherefore, Umar needs to exercise for 360 minutes on Saturday to reach his goal.\n</think>\n<answer>\nUmar needs to exercise for 360 minutes on Saturday to reach his goal.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 360.0, "ground_truth": 400.0, "is_correct": false, "original_answer_text": "On Thursday and Friday he exercised a total of 40 minutes because 24 + 16 = 40\nOn Saturday he has to exercise for 400 minutes because 40 x 10 = 400\n#### 400"}
