{"dataset": "GSM_Original", "item_id": 736, "question": "Comet Encke orbits the sun every 50 years. Oliver's grandfather saw the Comet when he was 28 years old. Oliver saw the comet a second time when he was two times the age his grandfather was when he saw the Comet. How old was Oliver when he saw the Comet for the first time?", "prompt": "As an expert problem solver, solve step by step the following mathematical questions. Comet Encke orbits the sun every 50 years. Oliver's grandfather saw the Comet when he was 28 years old. Oliver saw the comet a second time when he was two times the age his grandfather was when he saw the Comet. How old was Oliver when he saw the Comet for the first time?", "model_response": "<think>\nTo solve this problem, we need to break it down into several steps and use the given information to find the solution. Let's denote the following variables:\n- \\( T \\): The age of Oliver's grandfather when he saw the Comet for the first time.\n- \\( O \\): Oliver's age when he saw the Comet for the first time.\n- \\( G \\): Oliver's grandfather's age when Oliver saw the Comet for the first time.\n- \\( O_2 \\): Oliver's age when he saw the Comet for the second time.\n- \\( G_2 \\): Oliver's grandfather's age when Oliver saw the Comet for the second time.\n\nFrom the problem, we know:\n1. Comet Encke orbits the sun every 50 years.\n2. Oliver's grandfather saw the Comet when he was 28 years old.\n3. Oliver saw the comet a second time when he was two times the age his grandfather was when he saw the Comet.\n\nFirst, let's determine the age of Oliver's grandfather when he saw the Comet for the first time:\n\\[ T = 28 \\]\n\nNext, we need to find Oliver's age when he saw the Comet for the second time. According to the problem, Oliver saw the comet a second time when he was two times the age his grandfather was when he saw the Comet:\n\\[ O_2 = 2 \\times T = 2 \\times 28 = 56 \\]\n\nNow, we need to determine how many years passed between the first and second sightings of the Comet. Since Comet Encke orbits the sun every 50 years, the time between sightings is:\n\\[ \\text{Time between sightings} = 50 \\text{ years} \\]\n\nLet's denote the age of Oliver's grandfather when Oliver saw the Comet for the second time as \\( G_2 \\). Since 50 years have passed since the first sighting:\n\\[ G_2 = T + 50 = 28 + 50 = 78 \\]\n\nWe know that Oliver saw the comet for the second time when he was 56 years old. Therefore, we can find Oliver's age when he saw the Comet for the first time by subtracting the time between sightings from his age at the second sighting:\n\\[ O = O_2 - \\text{Time between sightings} = 56 - 50 = 6 \\]\n\nThus, Oliver was 6 years old when he saw the Comet for the first time.\n</think>\n<answer>\nOliver was 6 years old when he saw the Comet for the first time.\n</answer>", "model_answer": 6.0, "ground_truth": 6.0, "is_correct": true, "original_answer_text": "Oliver saw the Comet for the second time when he was 28 years * 2= 56 years old.\nComet Encke can be seen every 50 years, so Oliver saw the comet for the first time when he was 56 years - 50 years = 6 years old.\n#### 6"}
